# TypeScript & JavaScript Rules

## Code Style
- Use 2-space indentation
- Max line length: 100 characters
- Always use semicolons
- Prefer `const` over `let`, never use `var`
- Explicit return types on exported functions
- Use named exports, avoid default exports

## TypeScript Guidelines
- Strict mode compatibility required
- Explicit types for all props and state
- Use proper TypeScript interfaces for API responses
- Type all function parameters and return values
- Use proper generic types where applicable

## Error Handling
- Use try-catch blocks for async operations
- Implement proper error boundaries in React
- Return standardized error objects from API
- Log errors appropriately for debugging
- Use [src/services/errorHandler.js](mdc:src/services/errorHandler.js) for consistent error handling

## Performance
- Use React.memo() for expensive components
- Implement proper dependency arrays in useEffect
- Use useCallback for event handlers passed to children
- Lazy load components and routes
- Optimize bundle size with code splitting

## Modern JavaScript
- Use ES6+ features (arrow functions, destructuring, template literals)
- Prefer async/await over Promise chains
- Use optional chaining and nullish coalescing
- Implement proper cleanup in useEffect hooks